<div class="row align-items-start mt-4">
  <!-- Text -->
  <div class="col-md-7">
    <h2 class="h4 mb-3">Opportunities</h2>
    <p>
      The SFU AIRob Lab is always looking for self-motivated students at all levels. If you are interested in working with us on AI, robotics, and
      multi-agent/robot systems, please mention lab director
      <strong>Hang Ma</strong> in your application to the SFU CS graduate program.
    </p>
    <p>
      Applicants should also refer to the
      <a href="http://www.sfu.ca/computing/prospective-students/graduate-students.html" target="_blank"> SFU CS graduate program page </a>
      for more information on the
      <a href="http://www.sfu.ca/computing/prospective-students/graduate-students/admissions/requirements.html" target="_blank">
        admission requirements
      </a>
      and
      <a href="http://www.sfu.ca/computing/prospective-students/graduate-students/admissions/online-application.html" target="_blank">
        application deadlines </a
      >. Eligible students with only a bachelor’s degree are encouraged to apply directly to the PhD program.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4 mb-3">Location</h2>
    <p>
      The
      <a href="https://www.sfu.ca/campuses/maps-and-directions/burnaby-map.html" target="_blank"> SFU Burnaby campus </a>
      is located on Burnaby Mountain, about 12 miles from downtown Vancouver, offering easy access to a vibrant metropolitan area while being
      surrounded by nature.
    </p>
  </div>

